+
+The tooltip dispatches the following events on its trigger. Each one bubbles and carries no detail,
+which the platform reads as `null`.
+
+| Key        | Wire name             | Cancelable | Dispatched                                                   |
+| ---------- | --------------------- | ---------- | ------------------------------------------------------------ |
+| `show`     | `show.vn.tooltip`     | Yes        | Before the tip is built; prevention refuses the show         |
+| `inserted` | `inserted.vn.tooltip` | No         | After the tip enters its container                           |
+| `shown`    | `shown.vn.tooltip`    | No         | After the tip's transitions settle                           |
+| `hide`     | `hide.vn.tooltip`     | Yes        | Before the `shown` token leaves; prevention refuses the hide |
+| `hidden`   | `hidden.vn.tooltip`   | No         | After the tip leaves its container                           |
+
+A show takes its identity before it dispatches `show.vn.tooltip`, so a show a listener starts inside
+that dispatch resolves `false` as in flight, and a hide takes a show in flight over. After each
+write, dispatch, and await, a call reads its lifetime and whether it still holds its change and the
+tip it built; a show also reads that the tip is in its container after the insertion and the
+`inserted.vn.tooltip` event and that it carries the `shown` token after that write and after the
+wait, and a hide reads that the tip lacks the `shown` token after its removal and after the wait. A
+call that finds the tooltip destroyed, a later call started, or the tip otherwise stops, writing and
+dispatching nothing more, and resolves `false`. When a listener refuses the tip's promotion, the
+show removes the tip it built and resolves `false`. Destruction clears the timer, abandons a wait in
+flight, restores the placement, removes the tip with no event, and restores the trigger's `title`,
+`aria-label`, and `aria-describedby` attributes. An aborted `signal` destroys the tooltip, and so
+does one that aborts while construction runs.
+
+The tooltip departs from Bootstrap's in these ways:
+
+- The events carry the `.vn.` namespace, such as `shown.vn.tooltip`, where Bootstrap's carry `.bs.`,
+  and the completed events are not cancelable.
+- The option Bootstrap names `animation` is `animated`, `customClass` is `tip.class`, a string of
+  class tokens with no function form, `template` is `tip.template`, `selector` is `descendants`, and
+  `fallbackPlacements` is `placement.fallbacks`. The trigger words become the `trigger` group, and a
+  delay given as one number fills the `delay` group. The `placement` and `offset` options take no
+  function, and no `data-bs-config` attribute is read.
+- The `sanitize`, `sanitizeFn`, `allowList`, `boundary`, and `popperConfig` options have no
+  counterpart.
+- No `data-bs-original-title` attribute is written: the tooltip keeps the trigger's title itself and
+  restores the `title` attribute on destruction.
+- The tip is placed through CSS anchor positioning in the top layer through the `hint` popover
+  value, so the `container` option receives the tip element while the platform positions it, and the
+  platform closes the tip on Escape, on a click outside it, and when another tooltip's tip opens.
+  Bootstrap places the tip through Popper inside its container, and any number of its tips show at
+  once.
+- The container defaults to the nearest ancestor carrying `aria-modal="true"`, else the body.
+  Bootstrap's defaults to the body.
+- The trigger's `aria-describedby` attribute keeps every other id it carries. Bootstrap's `show`
+  method overwrites the attribute, and its `hide` method removes it.
+- A show resolves `false` while a change is in flight and for a trigger whose inline `display` is
+  `none`. Bootstrap's `show` method runs again in flight and throws for that trigger.
+- The tooltip has content when any slot has content. Bootstrap's tooltip reads its title alone.
+- A `title` option that resolves empty leaves the title slot empty. Bootstrap's tooltip then falls
+  back to the trigger's original `title` attribute.
+- An element content is moved into its slot whatever the `html` option reads. Bootstrap's template
+  factory copies the element's text when `html` is `false`.
+- A descendant's tooltip takes the options you passed the container. Bootstrap's takes every
+  container option that differs from its default, the container's data attributes included.
+- A `data-bs-trigger` word other than `hover`, `focus`, `click`, and `manual` is refused, so the
+  tooltip throws on it. Bootstrap reads any other word as a focus trigger.
+- No `toggleEnabled` method exists: call `enable` or `disable`, and read `enabled`.
